<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#prince-of-transylvania">Glossary</a> · Term · title</p><h1 class="enc-title">Prince of Transylvania</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1570–1711</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Prince of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transylvania">Transylvania</a> was the title of the rulers of the Principality of Transylvania, first taken by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-sigismund-zapolya">John Sigismund Zápolya</a> when he gave up the Hungarian royal title at the Treaty of Speyer in 1570. The princes were elected by the Transylvanian diet and ruled under Ottoman suzerainty until the principality passed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a> at the end of the 17th century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/prince-of-transylvania.jpg" alt="Prince of Transylvania" width="320" height="362" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dahn · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arms_of_Transylvania_in_Cod._icon._391.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
